KPL/SCLK

SYNTHETIC spacecraft clock kernel for spice-lite tests. This is not a real
mission clock and must never be used for anything but testing. It was written
by hand for test/sclk.test.mjs to exercise a clock reset: partition 2 starts
again at count zero, so the same clock reading occurs in both partitions and
one host time base cannot cover both.

Clock -902 has two fields: a count of nominal seconds and a count of
milliseconds. It runs on TT (time system 2). Zero is at 141000000 TT seconds
past J2000 (2004-06-20). Partition 1 covers clock counts 0 to 1500000; the
clock then restarts at zero and runs slightly fast.

\begindata
SCLK_KERNEL_ID            = ( @2026-11-20T00:00:00 )
SCLK_DATA_TYPE_902        = ( 1 )
SCLK01_TIME_SYSTEM_902    = ( 2 )
SCLK01_N_FIELDS_902       = ( 2 )
SCLK01_MODULI_902         = ( 4294967296 1000 )
SCLK01_OFFSETS_902        = ( 0 0 )
SCLK01_OUTPUT_DELIM_902   = ( 1 )
SCLK_PARTITION_START_902  = ( 0.0000000000000E+00
                              0.0000000000000E+00 )
SCLK_PARTITION_END_902    = ( 1.5000000000000E+09
                              1.0000000000000E+13 )
SCLK01_COEFFICIENTS_902   = ( 0.0000000000000E+00  1.4100000000000E+08  1.0000000000000E+00
                              1.5000000000000E+09  1.4250000000000E+08  1.0000001000000E+00 )
\begintext
